From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: the stepped prompt pass in its own file beside cuda_lanes.zig

zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig is 600 lines at v1.2.7, the lean rule's limit, and the knobs later in this
series add lines to Lanes.facts(). Lanes.prefillStep and its vtable entry move, unchanged, to
cuda_lanes_step.zig (the fold did the same move inside its reply-prefill patch, which this re-seat defers);
Lanes keeps the name as an alias, and the helpers the step calls (of, take, cancelled, opening, images, marksOf,
Sink) are made pub. No behaviour changes: the same body, called from the same vtable slot.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat:
- cuda_lanes.zig 600 -> 570 lines; zig/prefill_widths_glm_host.zig still calls glm.lanes.Lanes.prefillStep.

